{"step_index":211,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T10:18:19Z","input_tokens":2113,"cache_read_tokens":298932,"output_tokens":4352,"thinking":"Initial focus is on generating a demo image for the new game mechanic. The user wants the image generated first. The first mechanic element is to keep the current map section unchanged at the top of the image.\n\n\nThe image should depict a pixel art mushroom with vertical columns of overlaid cards. Each column's cards of the same color are enclosed in a common outline at the base. Four slots will be at the bottom for card collection. Clicking a column transfers all cards of the same color from that column to the matching (or empty) slot below, stacking them like a deck with 3D depth and showing the card count beneath each slot.\n\n\nInitial image generation focuses on pixel art mushroom with overlaid card columns. Each column will have cards of the same color, enclosed in a common outline at the base. Four slots at the bottom are for card collection. Clicking a column moves all cards of the same color to the matching (or empty) slot, stacking them with 3D depth and card count display.\n\nThe game mechanic hinges on clearing cards from columns to slots. Card clears happen when the stack is full (e.g., \"8 / 8\"). If a column is clicked and no matching or empty slot exists, the system searches for another column with a matching bottom card to merge, uncovering hidden cards. Game win condition is clearing all cards; loss is when no moves are possible (full slots of incomplete colors and no matching column bases).\n\n\nThe four slots at the bottom are the deck collectors. The player will no longer need to view column counts, since the clear target is fixed beneath each slot.\n\nWhen all four slots are full of distinct colors, a column click merges with a matching column on the game board. This twist combines elements of \"Screw Jam / Bus Jam\" with \"Solitaire Card Sort\". Even if the slots are filled with four colors, merging columns on the board reveals hidden cards.\n\n\nThe image will showcase a pixel art mushroom map with six columns of cards, each with a unified outline around the bottom group of the same color. The top right will feature \"Undo\" and \"Reset\" buttons. Clear visual cues will illustrate the card flow: clicking a column moves cards to matching/empty slots or merges horizontally with another matching column when all slots are filled. Four slots will be arranged at the bottom, depicting 3D stacked decks of cards.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"import os\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw, ImageFont\n\nW, H = 720, 1600\nimg = Image.new('RGB', (W, H), '#05130a')\nd = ImageDraw.Draw(img)\n\n# Fonts\nfont_btn = ImageFont.truetype('C:/Windows/Fonts/segoeuib.ttf', 26)\nfont_counter = ImageFont.truetype('C:/Windows/Fonts/segoeuib.ttf', 24)\nfont_slot_empty = ImageFont.truetype('C:/Windows/Fonts/segoeuib.ttf', 18)\nfont_note = ImageFont.truetype('C:/Windows/Fonts/segoeuib.ttf', 18)\n\n# 1. Felt Game Board Frame (720 x 1600)\nd.rounded_rectangle([8, 8, W - 8, H - 8], radius=40, fill='#114b29', outline='#082313', width=8)\nd.rounded_rectangle([18, 18, W - 18, H - 18], radius=34, fill='#145a32', outline='#0d3d22', width=3)\n\n# 2. Top Right Buttons Only (Undo & Reset)\nbtn_y = 42\n# Undo\nd.ellipse([W - 170, btn_y, W - 106, btn_y + 64], fill='#092614', outline='#ffffff55', width=2)\nd.text((W - 151, btn_y + 13), \"↩\", fill='#ffffff', font=font_btn)\n# Reset\nd.ellipse([W - 92, btn_y, W - 28, btn_y + 64], fill='#092614', outline='#ffffff55', width=2)\nd.text((W - 73, btn_y + 13), \"⟳\", fill='#ffffff', font=font_btn)\n\n# 3. 6-Column Pixel Art Map (Unified Black 'D')\nCOLORS = {\n    'D': {'fill': (24, 24, 27),    'border': (63, 63, 70),    'hi': (113, 113, 122)},\n    'R': {'fill': (239, 68, 68),   'border': (185, 28, 28),   'hi': (252, 165, 165)},\n    'W': {'fill': (248, 250, 252), 'border': (148, 163, 184), 'hi': (255, 255, 255)},\n    'S': {'fill': (254, 215, 170), 'border': (217, 119, 6),   'hi': (255, 237, 213)},\n    'G': {'fill': (34, 197, 94),   'border': (21, 128, 61),   'hi': (134, 239, 172)},\n    'Y': {'fill': (234, 179, 8),   'border': (161, 98, 7),    'hi': (254, 240, 138)}\n}\n\nGRID_6X16 = [\n    'DDRRDD',\n    'DRRRRD',\n    'RRWWRR',\n    'RRWWRR',\n    'WRRRRW',\n    'WRRRRW',\n    'RRRRRR',\n    'DSSSSD',\n    'DDSSDD',\n    'DDSSDD',\n    'DSSSSD',\n    'DGGGGD',\n    'GGGGGG',\n    'GGGGGG',\n    'GGYYGG',\n    'GYGGYG'\n]\n\n# Build columns\ncols = [[], [], [], [], [], []]\nfor r in range(len(GRID_6X16)):\n    for c in range(6):\n        cols[c].append(GRID_6X16[r][c])\n\nCARD_W = 102\nCARD_H = 164\nCOL_GAP = 10\nSTEP_Y = 44\nSTART_X = (W - (6 * CARD_W + 5 * COL_GAP)) // 2\nSTART_Y = 130\n\ndef get_bottom_group_count(col):\n    if not col:\n        return 0\n    color = col[-1]\n    k = 0\n    for i in range(len(col) - 1, -1, -1):\n        if col[i] == color:\n            k += 1\n        else:\n            break\n    return k\n\ndef draw_single_card(x, y, w, h, c_key, shadow_off=4):\n    c = COLORS[c_key]\n    d.rounded_rectangle([x + 2, y + shadow_off, x + w + 2, y + h + shadow_off], radius=13, fill=(0, 0, 0, 110))\n    d.rounded_rectangle([x, y, x + w, y + h], radius=13, fill=c['fill'], outline=c['border'], width=2)\n    d.line([x + 8, y + 3, x + w - 8, y + 3], fill=c['hi'], width=2)\n\nfor c_idx in range(6):\n    col = cols[c_idx]\n    cx = START_X + c_idx * (CARD_W + COL_GAP)\n    grp_count = get_bottom_group_count(col)\n    upper_count = len(col) - grp_count\n\n    # Draw upper cards\n    for i in range(upper_count):\n        cy = START_Y + i * STEP_Y\n        draw_single_card(cx, cy, CARD_W, CARD_H, col[i], shadow_off=3)\n\n    # Draw bottom group cards\n    for g in range(grp_count):\n        idx = upper_count + g\n        cy = START_Y + idx * STEP_Y\n        draw_single_card(cx, cy, CARD_W, CARD_H, col[idx], shadow_off=5)\n\n    # Draw unified glowing outline around the entire bottom group!\n    grp_top = START_Y + upper_count * STEP_Y\n    grp_bottom = START_Y + (len(col) - 1) * STEP_Y + CARD_H\n    d.rounded_rectangle(\n        [cx - 2, grp_top - 2, cx + CARD_W + 2, grp_bottom + 2],\n        radius=15, outline='#ffffff', width=4\n    )\n\n# 4. Divider & Bottom 4-Slot Deck Area\nSLOT_SECTION_Y = 1140\nd.line([48, SLOT_SECTION_Y - 35, W - 48, SLOT_SECTION_Y - 35], fill='#ffffff22', width=2)\n\nSLOT_W = 136\nSLOT_H = 190\nSLOT_GAP = 24\nSLOTS_START_X = (W - (4 * SLOT_W + 3 * SLOT_GAP)) // 2\n\n# Demo states for the 4 Slots:\n# Slot 1: Green (6/8 cards stacked neatly like a deck)\n# Slot 2: Yellow (4/8 cards stacked neatly)\n# Slot 3: Red (7/8 cards stacked neatly)\n# Slot 4: Empty (0/8)\nslots_demo = [\n    {'color': 'G', 'count': 6, 'target': 8},\n    {'color': 'Y', 'count': 4, 'target': 8},\n    {'color': 'R', 'count': 7, 'target': 8},\n    {'color': None, 'count': 0, 'target': 8}\n]\n\nfor s_idx, s_data in enumerate(slots_demo):\n    sx = SLOTS_START_X + s_idx * (SLOT_W + SLOT_GAP)\n    sy = SLOT_SECTION_Y\n\n    # Base slot tray\n    d.rounded_rectangle(\n        [sx, sy, sx + SLOT_W, sy + SLOT_H],\n        radius=16, fill='#0b321b', outline='#ffffff44', width=3\n    )\n\n    if s_data['color'] is None:\n        # Empty slot\n        d.text((sx + 34, sy + 80), \"SLOT\", fill='#ffffff33', font=font_slot_empty)\n        d.text((sx + 26, sy + 104), \"TRỐNG\", fill='#ffffff33', font=font_slot_empty)\n    else:\n        # Neat Deck Stack Effect: stack multiple slight vertical offsets (3px per card) from bottom up\n        c_key = s_data['color']\n        cnt = s_data['count']\n        deck_card_w = SLOT_W - 16\n        deck_card_h = SLOT_H - 34\n        base_x = sx + 8\n        base_y = sy + 20\n\n        # Draw stacked deck layers (up to cnt layers, each shifted up by 3px)\n        for layer in range(cnt):\n            ly = base_y - layer * 3\n            lx = base_x\n            c = COLORS[c_key]\n            # Card layer in deck\n            d.rounded_rectangle(\n                [lx, ly, lx + deck_card_w, ly + deck_card_h],\n                radius=12, fill=c['fill'], outline=c['border'], width=2\n            )\n            d.line([lx + 8, ly + 3, lx + deck_card_w - 8, ly + 3], fill=c['hi'], width=1)\n\n        # Highlight top card of the deck with crisp white border\n        top_y = base_y - (cnt - 1) * 3\n        d.rounded_rectangle(\n            [base_x, top_y, base_x + deck_card_w, top_y + deck_card_h],\n            radius=12, outline='#ffffff', width=2\n        )\n\n    # Counter & Progress Bar BELOW each Slot (\"Phía dưới slot có số lá bài cần để clear\")\n    counter_y = sy + SLOT_H + 16\n    pill_w = SLOT_W\n    pill_h = 54\n    d.rounded_rectangle(\n        [sx, counter_y, sx + pill_w, counter_y + pill_h],\n        radius=14, fill='#082313', outline='#facc15' if s_data['color'] else '#ffffff33', width=2\n    )\n\n    txt = f\"{s_data['count']} / {s_data['target']}\"\n    d.text((sx + 38, counter_y + 6), txt, fill='#fef08a' if s_data['color'] else '#ffffff66', font=font_counter)\n\n    # Progress bar inside bottom counter box\n    bar_x = sx + 14\n    bar_y = counter_y + 38\n    bar_w = pill_w - 28\n    bar_h = 8\n    d.rounded_rectangle([bar_x, bar_y, bar_x + bar_w, bar_y + bar_h], radius=4, fill='#00000088')\n    if s_data['count'] > 0:\n        fill_w = int(bar_w * (s_data['count'] / s_data['target']))\n        d.rounded_rectangle([bar_x, bar_y, bar_x + fill_w, bar_y + bar_h], radius=4, fill='#4ade80')\n\nout_path = r'C:\\Users\\Admin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\0ca39d47-bf1d-4d04-97dc-9c2fe64cb8c8\\demo_4_slots_deck_collector.png'\nimg.save(out_path, quality=95)\nprint(\"SUCCESS:\", out_path, os.path.getsize(out_path))\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\Admin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\0ca39d47-bf1d-4d04-97dc-9c2fe64cb8c8\\gen_4slots_demo.py"}}]}
