{"step_index":221,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T10:21:11Z","input_tokens":2895,"cache_read_tokens":305701,"output_tokens":2217,"thinking":"The task is to implement the new card sorting mechanic into a standalone HTML demo, ensuring all rules of the 4-Slot Deck Collector + Column Merge hybrid are accurately represented. Starting with an evaluation of the existing map display, the design incorporates a new column-merge capability for dynamic game interaction.\n\n\nThe design requires a 6-column x 16-row layout with a fixed vertical screen size (720x1600). Implementation involves removing top text elements and retaining only the Undo and Reset buttons. Card dimensions are specified as 102x164, with a white outline for same-color card groups at the bottom. Below the map, there are 4 slots showing the current number of cards/required cards (k/Target) with a progress bar. Each slot will display card stacks in a 3D deck-like presentation.\n\nWhen a column is clicked, the system prioritizes moving the bottom card group ($k$ cards of color $C$) to a matching color slot or an empty one.\n\n\nNeed is calculated to determine how many cards are required to fill a slot, but the system should only take the precise amount needed, leaving excess cards. For instance, if a slot requires two more cards but the column has five of the correct color, only two cards should be moved to avoid overfilling and ensure correct clearing of the slot. Taking `min(count, target - slot.count)` cards from the column, then clearing a slot when it's full and empty.\n\n\nIf a column has excess cards of the target color after moving the required amount, those cards remain. Considering the scenario of two slots containing the same color, the design prioritizes moving cards to a slot with the same color, preventing this situation. This is ensured because the system first seeks a slot with the same color and only uses an empty slot if no same-color slot exists. The system only takes the needed cards, leaving the remainder in the column, hence a color only ever occupies one slot at a time. If no matching or empty slots are available, prioritize moving to another map column with the same final card color. Otherwise, move the entire $k$ cards to that other column to reveal the card on top of the original column.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"node -e \"\nconst MAX_BATCH = 8;\nconst GRID_6X16 = [\n  'DDRRDD',\n  'DRRRRD',\n  'RRWWRR',\n  'RRWWRR',\n  'WRRRRW',\n  'WRRRRW',\n  'RRRRRR',\n  'DSSSSD',\n  'DDSSDD',\n  'DDSSDD',\n  'DSSSSD',\n  'DGGGGD',\n  'GGGGGG',\n  'GGGGGG',\n  'GGYYGG',\n  'GYGGYG'\n];\n\nfunction buildCols(grid) {\n  const cols = [[], [], [], [], [], []];\n  for (let r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < 6; c++) cols[c].push(grid[r][c]);\n  }\n  return cols;\n}\nfunction getBottomGroupCount(col) {\n  if (col.length === 0) return 0;\n  const color = col[col.length - 1];\n  let k = 0;\n  for (let i = col.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n    if (col[i] === color) k++; else break;\n  }\n  return k;\n}\nfunction getTotalRem(cols, slots, color) {\n  let t = 0;\n  for (const col of cols) for (const c of col) if (c === color) t++;\n  for (const s of slots) if (s && s.color === color) t += s.count;\n  return t;\n}\nfunction getTarget(cols, slots, color) {\n  return Math.min(MAX_BATCH, Math.max(1, getTotalRem(cols, slots, color)));\n}\nfunction stepCol(state, colIdx) {\n  const cols = state.cols.map(c => [...c]);\n  const slots = state.slots.map(s => s ? { ...s } : null);\n  const col = cols[colIdx];\n  if (col.length === 0) return null;\n  const count = getBottomGroupCount(col);\n  const color = col[col.length - 1];\n\n  // Priority 1: Matching slot or Empty slot\n  let sIdx = slots.findIndex(s => s && s.color === color);\n  if (sIdx === -1) sIdx = slots.findIndex(s => s === null);\n\n  if (sIdx !== -1) {\n    const target = getTarget(cols, slots, color);\n    const cur = slots[sIdx] ? slots[sIdx].count : 0;\n    const need = target - cur;\n    const take = Math.min(count, need);\n    col.splice(col.length - take, take);\n    if (!slots[sIdx]) slots[sIdx] = { color, count: take };\n    else slots[sIdx].count += take;\n    if (slots[sIdx].count >= target) {\n      slots[sIdx] = null;\n    }\n    return { cols, slots };\n  }\n\n  // Priority 2: Another column with matching bottom color\n  const n = cols.length;\n  for (let s = 1; s < n; s++) {\n    const idx = (colIdx + s) % n;\n    if (cols[idx].length > 0 && cols[idx][cols[idx].length - 1] === color) {\n      col.splice(col.length - count, count);\n      for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) cols[idx].push(color);\n      return { cols, slots };\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nlet state = { cols: buildCols(GRID_6X16), slots: [null, null, null, null] };\n// Greedy simulation test\nlet moves = 0;\nwhile (moves < 100) {\n  const rem = state.cols.reduce((a, c) => a + c.length, 0) + state.slots.reduce((a, s) => a + (s ? s.count : 0), 0);\n  if (rem === 0) { console.log('WIN in', moves, 'moves!'); break; }\n  let moved = false;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\n    const next = stepCol(state, i);\n    if (next) { state = next; moves++; moved = true; break; }\n  }\n  if (!moved) { console.log('Stuck at move', moves); break; }\n}\n\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Verify 4-Slot Deck Collector gameplay simulation"}}]}
